{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Run one command line on a remote host over ssh (BatchMode=yes, key auth only — never prompts). Returns FLAT {ok, exit_code, stdout, stderr}; a spawn failure or auth failure lands in stderr with exit_code -1/255 rather than hanging. timeout_secs is the connect timeout (0 = 10s default); it does not bound the remote command's runtime.","import":"use std::process::Command;","params":[{"desc":"SSH target as user@host or a bare host/alias resolvable by ~/.ssh/config (e.g. mraiser@10.1.10.233).","name":"host","type":"String"},{"desc":"The shell command line to run on the remote host (passed as one argument to ssh, so the remote shell interprets it).","name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"desc":"Connection timeout in seconds passed to ssh -o ConnectTimeout. Pass 0 for the default of 10.","name":"timeout_secs","type":"Integer"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"lqmggg1a038e57681y2","readers":[],"time":1787660985069,"username":"system","writers":[]}